  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: you're_so_old_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts an elderly man dressed as a biblical figure holding a gravestone with the Ten Commandments, overlaid with the text 'you're so old' and 'this was your first school book.' The intent is to mock older individuals by implying their foundational knowledge or values are outdated or simplistic, using age as a target. While not explicitly targeting a protected group, it is ageist and potentially harmful by reducing the value of older people's experience and wisdom to a childish or archaic level. The juxtaposition of the gravestone (symbolizing death or finality) with the Ten Commandments (a foundational text) and the mocking text creates a humorous but demeaning portrayal of aging, which can be hurtful to older individuals.",
